Decision: **AVOID at conviction 3.** The scorecard totals 8 points, one short of the 9 needed for a buy. Quality, its direction and the balance sheet all get full marks, but the discount to the value blend is only about 14%, the moat is narrow and the branded-checkout risk is medium.

Things you should know:
- **Price basis:** the rules make me score on the last completed close (57.89 on 2026-11-18), not the 56.835 intraday price. At 56.835 the discount would likely reach the next band and give conviction 4. The new entry price is 57.42 (base fair value 67.56 × 0.85), so the stock sits just around it. The watch will probably fire again and trigger another full re-research rather than a buy.
- **Debt trigger is text-only now:** the statistics page shows debt/EBITDA at 2.13x on its definition, so a 1.5x check would already be true. The trigger now tracks net debt/EBITDA (0.61x today) and the weekly reviewer has to test it by hand.

I did not read the 2026-10-07 evaluation; it is more than 30 days old, so no new-evidence field is needed. Replacements were not considered because this is an AVOID.
